{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-112368",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We can introduce a new variable $z={h}^{2}$ and then rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{h}^{4}-13{h}^{2}-10 & =3{({h}^{2})}^{2}-13({h}^{2})-10 \\\\  & =3{z}^{2}-13z-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the quadratic, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of $h:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{z}^{2}-13z-10 & =(3z+2)(z-5) \\\\  & =(3{h}^{2}+2)({h}^{2}-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
